Objective

Access an administrator panel that was not properly protected and use the exposed administrative functionality to delete the user "carlos".

Methodology

I started by exploring the lab application.

I checked the site's "robots.txt" file:

"/robots.txt"

The response contained:

"Disallow: /administrator-panel"

This revealed the location of the administrator panel.

I then navigated directly to:

"/administrator-panel"

Instead of receiving an authorization error, the application displayed the administrator functionality.

The panel showed a list of users, including:

- "wiener"
- "carlos"

Each user had a Delete option.

I selected the Delete option for "carlos".

The application responded:

User deleted successfully!

